  "result": "I've written all three plan files, and the validator accepts every node. One law, NRS-484B-587-2a, is now deliberately blocked: I filed two gaps that need your decision before it can be coded.\n\n- **NRS-484B-363-4.** The failing witness was the \"blind\" test, which hides one input from the source and expects the rule to report unknown. Hiding vehicle position made the rule unknown for other reasons, and hiding bearing in iteration 2 changed nothing. It now hides the body-overlap input, which the overtaking concept reads directly, so hiding it alone makes the verdict unknown. The scenario text also now says the recording starts early enough that the look-back window isn't cut off. Nothing else in the record changed.\n\n- **NRS-484B-587-2a.** The gate flagged the \"authorized emergency vehicle\" condition as never exercised. That's because the run's reading classifies every vehicle class as unresolved under that group, so membership is always unknown and no witness can make it decide. The earlier gate results suggest the \"tow car\" group has the same problem, though that one is my reading of the gate output rather than something the feedback states outright. Swapping in a nearby class, or dropping the vehicle list, would change what the law says. So I added atom gaps on span e12 (authorized emergency vehicle; e13 relies on the same group) and span e15 (tow car). Another coding attempt would most likely have spent the law's last attempt and closed it as failed.\n\n- **NRS-484B-777-1, node o1.** It was returned only because the speed rule it relies on, `NRS_484B_785_1a`, was revised and re-accepted. The plan is unchanged and now uses the current version of that rule. The already-accepted node o2 is left alone.\n\nIn all three records I emptied the parameter proposals, since every parameter they use is now in the catalogue.\n\n**Decision for you:** to unblock 587-2a, either add class atoms or decide which vehicle classes count under the two groups. For example:\n- **Authorized emergency vehicle:** include `ru.emergency_vehicle` and `ru.fire_apparatus`. This is the same decision G86 already asks for, so making it once unblocks the other affected laws too.\n- **Tow car:** include `ru.official_vehicle` of kind tow, and exclude the bus classes.\n\nThese points are also in the \"For the operator\" section of `PLAN.md`.\n\nFiles are in `iter-004/plan/batch-03/`:\n- `blueprint.jsonl`\n- `PLAN.md`\n- `aggregates.jsonl` (empty, since none of these laws defines its own vehicle group)",
